WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.000
The GP (General Practitioner) is your NHS family doctor. The practice is called a «GP surgery» or «GP practice». Register as soon as you have an address; do not wait until you are ill. GP and nurse appointments are free, whatever your immigration status.

2
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:32.000
In England, the official guidance says practices do not have to ask you for proof of identity, address or immigration status, and cannot turn you away for not having it. Find a GP near your home with the «Find a GP» search on nhs.uk.

3
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Many practices have an online form; if not, go to reception.

4
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.200
Now do the lesson exercises. If you are unsure, watch this video again.
